<LegalLayout title="Privacy policy" eyebrow="Your information" description="This policy explains what BookMojo collects, why we use it and the choices available to you.">
  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>We may collect the purchaser’s name, email address, delivery address, order details and payment status. For personalisation, a parent or guardian may provide a child’s first name, age, appearance preferences, dedication and photograph.</p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <p>We use this information to create previews, fulfil and deliver orders, provide support, prevent fraud, maintain business records and comply with applicable law. We do not sell personal information.</p>

  <h2>Children’s information</h2>
  <p>Children’s details must be submitted by a parent, guardian or authorised adult. They are used only to create and fulfil the requested product. Please do not provide information that is not necessary for personalisation.</p>

  <h2>Photos and artwork</h2>
  <p>Submitted photos are used to guide the personalised illustration. We restrict access to people and service providers involved in production and delete source photos when they are no longer required for fulfilment, support or legal obligations.</p>

  <h2>Service providers and security</h2>
  <p>We may share only necessary information with payment, hosting, printing, communication and delivery providers. We use reasonable safeguards, but no online transmission or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure.</p>

  <h2>Retention and your choices</h2>
  <p>We retain order records only as long as reasonably needed for fulfilment, support, accounting and legal requirements. To request access, correction or deletion, email <a href="mailto:hello@bookmojo.in">hello@bookmojo.in</a>. Some records may need to be retained where required by law.</p>

  <h2>Policy updates</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy as our services or legal obligations change. The effective date above shows the latest revision.</p>
</LegalLayout>